				<r3d:description language="eng">GRIIDC is a multidisciplinary data repository based out of the Harte Research Institute at Texas A&amp;M University - Corpus Christi. GRIIDC stores data from multiple fields of study including biology, chemistry, physical oceanography, sociology, political science, and public health. Data are free to download and are issued digital object identifiers. Storage services are fee-based and include data management/submission training; data management planning assistance; and storage and distribution. The mission of GRIIDC is to ensure a data and information legacy that promotes continual scientific discovery and public awareness of coastal and marine ecosystems.</r3d:description>
